  Q("math-10", { paper: "P1", marks: 6, diff: 2, q: "A bag has 5 red and 3 blue counters. Two are taken without replacement.<br>(a) Complete a tree diagram. [2]<br>(b) Find P(both the same colour). [2]<br>(c) Given that they are the same colour, find P(both red). [2]", ms: ["(a) first draw \\(\\frac{5}{8}, \\frac{3}{8}\\); second \\(\\frac{4}{7}, \\frac{3}{7}\\) after red, \\(\\frac{5}{7}, \\frac{2}{7}\\) after blue [A1][A1]", "(b) \\(\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot\\frac{4}{7} + \\frac{3}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{7} = \\frac{26}{56} = \\frac{13}{28}\\) [M1][A1]", "(c) \\(\\frac{20/56}{26/56} = \\frac{10}{13}\\) [M1][A1]"] });
  Q("math-10", { paper: "P1", marks: 6, diff: 2, q: "In a class of 30 students, 18 study French (F), 12 study Spanish (S) and 5 study neither.<br>(a) Draw a Venn diagram and find how many study both. [3]<br>(b) A student who studies French is chosen at random. Find the probability that they also study Spanish. [3]", ms: ["(a) \\(18 + 12 - x + 5 = 30\\) [M1]", "\\(x = 5\\) [A1]; regions 13, 5, 7, 5 [A1]", "(b) \\(P(S \\mid F) = \\frac{5}{18}\\) [M1][A1][A1]"] });
  Q("math-10", { paper: "P1", marks: 5, diff: 2, q: "Events A and B are such that \\(P(A) = 0.4\\), \\(P(B) = 0.5\\) and \\(P(A \\cup B) = 0.7\\).<br>(a) Find \\(P(A \\cap B)\\). [2]<br>(b) Determine whether A and B are independent. [2]<br>(c) Find \\(P(A \\mid B')\\). [1]", ms: ["(a) \\(0.4 + 0.5 - 0.7 = 0.2\\) [M1][A1]", "(b) \\(P(A)P(B) = 0.2 = P(A \\cap B)\\) [M1] so independent [A1]", "(c) \\(P(A \\mid B') = P(A) = 0.4\\) [A1]"], numeric: { value: 0.2, tol: 0.001 } });
  Q("math-10", { paper: "P1", marks: 4, diff: 2, q: "Two fair six-sided dice are rolled and the scores are added. Using a sample-space diagram, find:<br>(a) P(total = 8) [2]<br>(b) P(total ≥ 10 | at least one die shows 6) [2]", ms: ["(a) 5 outcomes out of 36: \\(\\frac{5}{36}\\) [M1][A1]", "(b) 11 outcomes with a 6; of these, totals ≥ 10: (4,6),(5,6),(6,6),(6,4),(6,5) = 5 [M1]", "\\(\\frac{5}{11}\\) [A1]"] });
  Q("math-10", { paper: "P1", marks: 4, diff: 3, q: "\\(P(A) = 0.3\\), \\(P(B \\mid A) = 0.6\\) and \\(P(B \\mid A') = 0.2\\). Find \\(P(A \\mid B)\\).", ms: ["\\(P(B) = 0.3(0.6) + 0.7(0.2) = 0.32\\) [M1][A1]", "\\(P(A \\mid B) = \\frac{0.18}{0.32}\\) [M1]", "\\(= 0.5625 = \\frac{9}{16}\\) [A1]"], numeric: { value: 0.5625, tol: 0.001 } });

